r than  raising questions about diana's apparent  super strength  the incident only makes barbara aspire  to be like diana  even more down on his luck would be oil  tycoon maxwell lord  first appears on television screens in  the mall where diana stops the robbery  as he tries to convince folks that they  can improve their lives with the help of  his company  black gold cooperative despite the  glossy feel of his ads  maxwell is broke and his top investor  simon stagg  is getting angry desperate to make money  and support  as well as impress his young son  alistair  maxwell seeks out a rather unorthodox  fix  when he hears about the stone that  barbara and diana have discovered  the dreamstone he sees a way out of his  predicament  he comes up with a plan to use the  dreamstone for his own gains  seducing barbara to gain access to the  artifact for himself before max takes  possession of the stone  both diana and barbara wish upon it  though neither of them quite understand  what they're doing  diana wishes that steve could still be  with her the next day at a smithsonian  gala  she's taken aback when she discovers  that steve living in someone else's body  has indeed returned meanwhile barbara  wishes for the confidence and power of  her new friend diana  and begins to see a change almost  immediately she's suddenly striding  around the smithsonian  in slinky outfits and attracting  attention from everyone around her  at a gala maxwell invites her into a  room alone  but it's all a ruse to steal the dream  stone maxwell takes his wish  a huge step further too becoming the  stone himself  so he can grant anybody's wishes as well  as his own  with this power maxwell can manipulate  the entire world  making deals with international figures  and causing complete chaos  all three wishers eventually realize  there's a huge downside to the dream  stone  it steals your life essence when you  make a wish diana might be happy with  steve by her side  but her powers are fading she's unable  to harness her strength or  properly wield the lasso of truth  barbara completely loses the humanity  that drew diana to her in the first  place  driven only by vengeance and a thirst  for more strength and influence  you've always had everything well people  like me have had nothing  to make matters worse barbara makes more  wishes on the stone  through maxwell turning herself into the  animalistic  hyper-strong cheetah maxwell fares worst  of all  as he continues to grant wishes and  emotionally manipulate the world so he  has power over everybody  even the president of the united states  his body begins to break down  his nose and ears stream blood his eyes  are red  his body is visibly wrecked despite  these negative effects  everyone even diana is loathed to let go  of their wishes even when they discover  that the stone was created by the god of  treachery and mischief himself  but the only way to return to normal is  to recant  diana and steve realize there's only one  thing she can do to regain her power and  bring down  maxwell and barbara recant her wish  after yet  another emotional goodbye a sobbing  diana takes her wish back  and steve shuffles off this mortal coil  once again  with her full powers returned diana  discovers maxwell's plan to use a u.s  military broadcast system to speak to  the entire world so he can grant wishes  and mass  diana in the full splendor of the  ancient golden amazonian armor of  hysteria  defeats cheetah electrocuting her to  turn her back into barbara  she then confronts maxwell she wraps the  lasso of truth around him and speaks to  the world over the broadcast system  begging everyone to recant their wishes  they do  stopping a nuclear war as a result diana  also  uses the lasso to show maxwell a vision  of his young son alistair  convincing him to return to his family  at the beginning of the movie  a much younger diana competes in a hyper  athletic sporting event  though she is the youngest competitor by  far diana immediately takes first place  but when she's knocked off her horse at  a crucial moment all seems lost  but diana finds a secret shortcut  putting her firmly back in first place  when she returns to the arena her aunt  antiope disqualifies her  saying she cheated diana protests but  antiope tells her that her victory can't  be achieved by dishonesty  stressing that truth is of the utmost  importance she tells diana  no true hero is born from lies and  remember  greatness is not what you think diana is  disappointed in the moment but she takes  those lessons about truth and honesty  with her  antiope's message of honesty proves  especially important by the end of  wonder woman 1984  through all three characters and their  dreamstone wishes it's clear diana  barbara and maxwell are all pretending  to be somebody they're not  the stone exposes their greatest flaws  even as it gives them their hearts  desire  though it seems to people like barbara  that diana has zero problems in her  perfect life  diana's unwillingness to engage with  anybody in the wake of losing steve  is a front for her loneliness and a  craving for human connection  barbara rather than finding confidence  within herself tries to steal diana's  meanwhile maxwell wants to appear  powerful at any cost  despite the fact that he's broke and his  business is failing in the end  whether they're giving up true love  finding their own confidence  or reuniting with family diana barbara  and maxwell  understand that the stone despite its  seductive wish-granting abilities  can't actually help them at all only  honesty and clarity can lead to true  greatness  you can't take shortcuts in the  aftermath of maxwell's hostile takeover  and a narrowly averted nuclear war  the world seems to return to normal by  the holiday season  back in dc and alone once more diana  watches families  spend time together at a christmas  village and even without steve in her  life  she seems at peace however the clearest  example of diana's personal progress  comes when she finds herself face to  face with the man whose body steve  inhabited during his recent turn on  earth  rather than closing herself off diana  lets herself open up to this stranger  complimenting the outfit we saw steve  try on earlier and giving him a warm  smile before they part ways  whether they'll meet again isn't clear  but what's important is that diana  who was once so committed to being alone  is willing to make human connections  once again  letting steve go once and for all and  living life on her own terms  she also harnesses some impressive  superpowers mastering flying through the  clouds with ease  in the aftermath of her experience with  the stone she's even more powerful  throughout the film the audience and  diana learn about asteria  an ancient amazonian who sacrificed  herself  and her strength to protect the maschira  from the prying eyes of men  during the flashback to diana's  childhood her mother  queen hippolyta soothes her distraught  daughter by showing her the golden  statue of asteria  and telling the story of the brave  warrior who saved the island  when the audience gets a brief glimpse  of asteria herself  the actor playing her looks familiar and  for good reason  as she's played by linda carter who  played wonder woman on the small screen  in the 1970s  in a post credits sequence it's revealed  that asteria  like diana secretly lives among  humankind whether carter appears in a  future wonder woman installment remains  to be seen  but no matter what it's fascinating to  learn that diana  isn't alone and potentially has an  incredibly powerful ally nearby  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  the dc eu are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  you
 

